  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Leland Stanford Junior University obligated $697M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The university won 34 awards with an average award size of $20.5M, and obligations were down 5.9% year over year. The Department of Energy is the dominant buyer, obligating $677M so far in FY2026. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the dominant market with $682M in obligations. Multi-year obligations show FY21 $548M, FY22 $678M, FY23 $659M, FY24 $732M, FY25 $741M, and FY26 $697M. Other notable agency obligations include the Department of Veterans Affairs $11M, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration $5.2M, and the Department of Health and Human Services $4.3M. The Department of Defense and the Department of the Interior show much smaller obligations at $111K and $6K respectively. Additional NAICS markets with measurable obligations include Research and Development in Biotechnology $9.4M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) $2.9M, Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools $1.5M, Blood and Organ Banks $1.3M, and Testing Laboratories and Services $269K.",
